TurboFieldfare is a specialized inference runtime for the Gemma 4 26B-A4B model, engineered to operate within an extreme memory budget of approximately 2 GB on Apple Silicon Macs. The central constraint is the inability to load the full 14.3 GB model into RAM. To circumvent this, the system adopts a hybrid memory strategy: it keeps the shared expert weights and the FP16 KV cache resident in memory, while streaming the necessary routed expert weights from SSD on demand.

The runtime architecture divides data handling into two distinct phases. Resident data includes the core shared experts and the KV cache